 "summary": "The canonical post-PR surface is minimal and complete: no compatibility aliases (the moved `apply_sub_smul_pair` has one rewritten use), no `private` general infrastructure, bodies unexposed in the new `public section` files with `(rfl)` restatements bridging them, and each of `energy`, `spatialPart`, `spatialNorm`, `cosAngle`, `projOrthogonal` carries its def/apply/kernel/range/idempotence/interaction lemmas. Structural normal forms (`spatialPart_n`, `spatialPart_orthogonal_n`, `energy_spatialPart`, `spatialPart_spatialPart`, `spatialNorm_smul`, `energy_n`, `restFrameWit_n`, `energy_restFrameWit_apply`) carry `@[simp]` while the definitional unfoldings correctly do not.",
